    {
      "id": "2089501024557912315",
      "text": "Grok is very good at agentic tasks!",
      "created_at": "Mon Aug 17 23:53:59 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": null,
      "quoted": {
        "id": "2089366682083225893",
        "text": "Agentic work is where @grok 4.6 lands hardest, taking the top spot on the Artificial Analysis Agentic Index at 59, tied with Claude Opus 5 Max.\n\nThe index measures tool use, planning, autonomy and complex problem solving rather than single answers\n\nGrok 4.6 completes tasks in ~53 turns and ~0.5bn input tokens on average, against ~103 turns and ~2.0bn for Claude Opus 5 Max\n\nCost of $0.84 per task, putting it on the intelligence versus cost per task Pareto frontier\n\nEnterprises buying agents pay per completed task, not per benchmark point. Turn efficiency is what determines whether a long-running workflow is affordable at volume.\n\nTwo labs now sit at the top of this index with very different cost structures. Buyers get real choice on price for the first time in agentic deployment.",
